the town of veronika is one of the  loveliest on the island of Kirk  tomislav appendage is a chef at konoba  Lewton a local restaurant many of the  guests are tourists day-trippers eager  to savor the local cuisine  we have many dishes on our menu but our  meat dishes like Shiva Chi Chi and ples  covet say are especially popular with  tourists but we also have plenty of  guests who are open to new dishes and  who want to try our local specialties  besides tourism farming is a mainstay of  the local economy and almost every  family owns a small flock of sheep lamb  dishes typical for this part of the  Balkans are very popular at Kona Berluti  Tommy's la vía punch each likes to serve  goulash with homemade pasta called  Charlotte's in Croatian first mixed  together flour eggs and oil with a mix  hot water makes the dough nice and  smooth then knead the dough and allow it  to sit for 15 minutes  in the meantime chop the onions and cube  the meat the goulash can be made with  lamb mutton beef veal or pork saute the  onions and add tomato paste season with  salt pepper bay leaves and rosemary then  browned meat  zeliha mono then it's quenched with a  dry red red wine ads both color and  flavor after the alcohol is boiled off  add some warm water and bring to a  simmer then it's time to roll out the  pasta dough and cut it into equal sized  portions using your hands and a knitting  needle roll the dough carefully remove  the needle so there's a hole in the  middle because that way the pasta can  soak up the sauce that makes it even  tastier for the perfect accompaniment  round it all off with a glass of Sheila  Tina a dry white local wine  you
 

